Abstract:
In this article we relate the set of structure preserving equivalent martingale measures (\mathcal{M}^	extup{sp}) for financial models driven by semimartingales with conditionally independent increments to a set of measurable and integrable functions (\mathcal{Y}). More precisely, we prove that (\mathcal{M}^	extup{sp} 
ot = \emptyset) if and only if (\mathcal{Y}
ot = \emptyset), and connect the sets (\mathcal{M}^	extup{sp}) and (\mathcal{Y}) to the semimartingale characteristics of the driving process. In addition we consider integrated L'evy models with independent stochastic factors and time-changed L'evy models and derive mild explicit conditions for (\mathcal{M}^	extup{sp} 
ot = \emptyset).
